  - id: sangeeth-reveal-2026-08-11
    date: 2026-08-11
    what: >
      Third reveal card. Pure DATA — the only component work was two new
      capabilities the existing cards had never needed: a centred panel and
      framed corner art. Everything else came from the ServiceReveal config.
    assets_in_public_root_again: >
      Brief said public/assets/; all four were in public/ ROOT, 9.2 MB total.
      That is now four briefs in a row naming a directory that has never
      existed. ALWAYS glob for the basename before trusting the path.
      Optimised to 930 KB:
        initial-16x9 1376x768 -> 1100x614 (1.7915) 304 KB
        decor-top    1376x768 -> 1200x597 (2.0101) 300 KB
        family-bl    1376x768 ->  615x560 (1.0982) 163 KB
        couple-br    1376x768 ->  702x560 (1.2536) 163 KB
    THE_TWO_CORNER_PIECES_NEEDED_REAL_CROPPING: >
      Both shipped as an illustration occupying the left ~60% of a frame, with
      a white page to its right and a GREENISH-GREY surround (#c4ccbd) around
      the whole thing. Rendered as-is they would have been two grey rectangles.
      Content bounds found with a mask of "saturated OR dark", which ignores
      both the pale surround and the white page.
    EQUAL_WIDTHS_WOULD_HAVE_BROKEN_THE_SCALE_AGAIN: >
      Brief said max-w-[30%] for both. The crops are different shapes — 1.098
      and 1.254 — so equal widths render the family 14% taller than the couple.
      28 / 32 instead, in proportion to the aspects, puts both at 25.5% of card
      width in height. Verified equal at 99px (1280) and 77px (1024).
      This is the third time on this component that matching box WIDTHS has
      been the wrong instrument for matching apparent SIZE.
    two_new_config_capabilities:
      - "`panelAlign: 'left' | 'center'` — left when one corner is occupied and
        the copy retreats away from it; center when BOTH are, since there is no
        side to retreat to. Sangeeth is the first card with both corners AND a
        panel."
      - "`framed` on corner art — rounded + ring. The Weddings/Engagements
        corners sit on a ground matching the card, so their edges are invisible;
        the Sangeeth pieces are near-black night-stage scenes on a cream card
        and read as pasted screenshots without a deliberate frame. With `framed`
        the box already carries the art's ratio, so object-cover fills it exactly
        and the frame hugs the picture."
    verified: >
      tsc clean, next build clean 21/21, /services/[slug] 13.8 kB / 185 kB.
      No chips, no ordinals on any of the three. Overlap with decoration AND
      corner art is 0 for all three at all widths.
      1280 (389x626): S decor 193px @2.01 full-width uncropped, panel 53% and
      centred (91/91), corners 109x99 + 124x99 equal, gaps 20/29, 8 lines.
      W gaps 84/103, E gaps 52/58 — both unaffected by the new fields.
      1024 (304x627): S panel 52% centred, corners 85x77 + 97x77 equal,
      gaps 18/19, 11 lines.
      375: S 335x625, panel 54% centred, gaps 19/22, 10 lines. No h-scroll.
    THE_ROW_IS_NOW_626: >
      561 -> 626 at 1280, and Sangeeth is what sets it: a 193px full-height
      decoration plus 8 lines in a 53% column. At 1024 it is 11 lines.
      All three cards in row 1 stretch to match. The levers are widening
      panelPct, shortening the Sangeeth longDesc, or accepting it — flagged to
