  - id: hero-asymmetric-spec
    date: 2026-08-04
    decision: >
      Hero rebuilt to a written spec supplied by the user — the fifth and first
      one built from a concrete brief rather than inference. Asymmetric 12-col
      grid: an 8-col type block against a 4-col vertical index of the seven
      practices; statistics stripped from the headline area into a rule-divided
      bar pinned to the section's bottom boundary; near-black #0D0D0E ground.
      components/home/Hero.tsx and HeroBackdrop.tsx rewritten. globals.css gained
      .hero-glow-a / .hero-glow-b.
    status: current
    PALETTE_REVERSAL: >
      This spec REVERSES the earlier standing instruction "do not introduce
      neon colours or monospace/tech-HUD styling; keep the purple/gold/warm
      off-white palette". The user explicitly asked for font-mono indices, a
      `[ LABEL // PLACE ]` HUD strip, and a #0D0D0E base. Newer explicit
      instruction wins; it was flagged to them before building. Plum survives
      only as radial depth over the black, and gold is unchanged.
    THREE_SPEC_DEVIATIONS: >
      All three were required to ship something that is not broken. Told to the
      user.
      1. Section is `flex flex-col` with the grid as `flex-1`, NOT a
         `min-h-screen` grid. A min-h-screen grid plus a stats bar puts the bar a
         full viewport BELOW the fold, which contradicts "pinned at the bottom
         boundary of the hero".
      2. `min-h-[100svh]` not `min-h-screen` — vh is cropped by mobile browser
         chrome. Project-wide convention already.
      3. Both ends of the type scale are clamps, not flat Tailwind steps. See
         below; this is the important one.
    TYPE_SCALE_MUST_TRACK_THE_COLUMN: >
      "Creating Moments," renders 8.94x the font size. The 8-col track is only
      587px at 1024px, so the specified flat `lg:text-8xl` (96px, needs ~854px)
      wrapped BOTH authored lines inside their masks — four lines instead of
      two, section 893px against a 768px viewport. `lg:text-[clamp(3.5rem,5.9vw,
      6rem)]` tracks the column with ~6% spare and still reaches the specified
      6rem ceiling from ~1630px up.
      At the other end `text-4xl` is a FIXED 36px, so it overflowed the 24px
      gutters below ~366px viewport width. Same fix, `clamp(1.75rem,9.2vw,
      2.25rem)`, ceiling equal to text-4xl.
      6.3vw was tried first and still wrapped at 1024 — the margin was 1px.
      Do not raise either slope without re-measuring.
    HOW_TO_DETECT_WRAP: >
      Compare the two line boxes' heights. Equal means neither wrapped; the
      widest-word measurement alone will NOT catch it, because a wrapped line
      still reports each word inside the column.
    grid_rule_anchoring: >
      The vertical rule between columns is anchored to the right column at
      `-left-4` (half the gap-8), NOT positioned at a percentage of the section.
      A percentage cannot track a 12-col gap through the container's own padding
      and landed ~20px off. It mounts at T+0.0 with the ground while its
      contents wait for T+0.5, so the wrapper carries the rule and the inner
      <nav> carries the fade.
    motion: >
      T+0 ground and structural rules, T+0.3 headline word-by-word out of a
      per-line mask (y 40 -> 0), T+0.5 CTAs and practice index, T+0.65 stats.
      All offsets are from `base`, so HeroIntro still plays first; on a repeat
      client-side visit base collapses to 0.1s and the timeline is the spec's.
      Practice hover: a rule that extends inside a FIXED-WIDTH track, not an
      element that grows — a width animating from 0 shoves the label sideways.
    verified: >
      tsc clean, next build clean. Home 15.4 kB / 194 kB.
      Section height equals viewport exactly at 1920x1080, 1440x820, 1280x720,
      1024x768, 768x1024 and 375x812. No headline wrap and no horizontal
      overflow at 320 / 375 / 768 / 1024 / 1280 / 1440 / 1920.
      1440: headline 85px, stats bar 720-820 flush to the bottom edge, column
      rule at x=934 exactly midway between 918 and 950.
      1920: headline hits the specified 96px ceiling.
      font-mono resolves to the real ui-monospace stack (Tailwind v4 keeps its
      default --font-mono; the project @theme only overrides sans and serif).
      13 mono elements, 7 practice rows, 4 stat cells, 0 stats in the headline
      area, practice nav hidden below lg. All three hit-tests resolve.
    NOT_verified: >
      No animation observed — rAF does not fire in this browser. Every number
      above was measured with opacity and transform force-overridden.

