  - id: hero-stagelight-refine
    date: 2026-08-04
    status_note: REVERTED — see hero-refinement-reverted.
    decision: >
      components/home/HeroAperture.tsx is DELETED. The right-hand graphic is now
      three soft light shafts in HeroBackdrop plus a one-shot glow that crosses
      the frame on load. The hero base bar lost the statistics strip entirely and
      the practice list became a bordered-cell index. A masthead meta row was
      added at the top (label left, location right).
    status: current
    supersedes: hero-aperture-rebuild (same day)
    why: >
      User circled two regions in red. The dial was the first: thin 1px gold
      arcs and 36 tick marks at ~700px do not read as an object at that scale,
      they read as scattered debris — and because the headline now spans the full
      column, the dial was sitting ON the type rather than beside it. Soft light
      cannot fail that way; it has no edges to look accidental.
      The second was the base bar: three stacked rows of ~10px uppercase (seven
      practices, then SCROLL + four statistics + location) with no hierarchy — a
      wall of tiny type under an otherwise confident hero.
    NO_STATS_IN_HERO: >
      The statistics have now failed twice here — as a 2x2 grid of oversized gold
      numerals (the single most template-like element on the page) and as a
      crammed inline strip. StatsBand already presents them properly further down
      the SAME page, so the hero copy was duplicating it. Do not put them back.
      The `short` field added to data/site.ts stats for the strip was reverted
      with it.
    index_cells: >
      The practice list is bordered cells at 15px serif, not a flat run of 13px
      items — structure is what makes it read as a deliberate index. shrink-0
      keeps it scrollable on touch; lg:flex-auto lets the seven cells share the
      leftover width so the row reaches the right edge instead of stopping 212px
      short. flex-auto not flex-1: equal-basis cells come out narrower than
      "Workshops & Retreats" needs.
    shafts_transform_trap: >
      The .hero-shaft-* keyframes animate `transform` wholesale, which drops the
      Tailwind rotate utility the instant the animation starts and snaps the
      shafts upright. The rotation therefore lives in a --shaft-rotate custom
      property that the keyframes re-apply on every frame. Same trap applies to
      any future CSS animation layered on a Tailwind transform.
    line_split: >
      KineticHeadline gained `lineX` — per-line horizontal offset driven by the
      cursor, so the two lines lean apart and the type gets a plane of its own.
      It is applied to the MASK box, never inside it: the mask is overflow-hidden
      and translating the contents would slice the ends off the words.
      Deliberately POINTER-driven, not scroll-driven — a scroll-linked horizontal
      split would reintroduce exactly the per-element divergence that collapsed
      an earlier hero (see contracts.parallax_units).
    also: >
      The secondary CTA trailed a short grey rule that read as a stray line; it
      is now a ringed arrow that fills gold from the bottom on hover. Headline
      gains a scroll-linked scale (1 -> 0.94, origin left) — scale only ever
      shrinks, so unlike a translate it cannot push into the paragraph below.
    verified: >
      tsc clean, next build clean. Home 17.1 kB / 196 kB first load.
      1440x820: section exactly 820, headline 136px ending 42px inside the
      container, spine clears the headline by 37px, index cells sum to the full
      1168px column, no cell clipped.
      1280x720: section exactly 720 (was 754 before trimming — the taller index
      cells had pushed it past the fold).
      390x844: section exactly 844, headline 70.2px, 13px between CTA and index.
      375x812: section exactly 812, 5px gap — the tightest realistic phone, and
      the reason the secondary CTA is min-h-12 below sm (still over the 44px tap
      target). Header is 84px and the eyebrow sits at 99px, so pt-24 cannot be
      reduced to buy more.
      No horizontal overflow at any width tested.
    NOT_verified: >
      Still no animation observed — rAF does not fire in this browser, so all
      geometry above was measured with opacity and transform force-overridden.
      The light shafts, the load sweep, the line split and the sheen are
      CSS/DOM-verified only.
    revert_how: >
      HeroAperture.tsx is in the 2026-08-04 transcript. The stats strip and the
      flat practice rail are in the hero-aperture-rebuild entry's version of
