  - id: hero-aperture-rebuild
    date: 2026-08-04
    status_note: SUPERSEDED by hero-stagelight-refine. The aperture dial is gone.
    decision: >
      The home hero was rebuilt as a kinetic editorial masthead. New files:
      components/home/HeroAperture.tsx, components/home/KineticHeadline.tsx,
      lib/usePointerParallax.ts. HeroBackdrop rewritten again. The Spine lives
      inside Hero.tsx. StrokeText is GONE from the hero.
    status: current
    why: >
      "currently this hero section looks too generic ... i want modern,
      professional, brand grade". It was: eyebrow, big headline, sentence, two
      buttons, 2x2 grid of oversized gold statistics. That is the default agency
      hero shape and restyling does not rescue it — so the GEOMETRY changed, not
      the paint. This is the fourth hero. Do not regress toward that shape.
    composition: >
      · full-height spine down the left gutter with the brand set vertically
        ([writing-mode:vertical-rl] rotate-180) — an editorial device, and the
        single clearest signal this is not a landing-page template. lg+ only;
        below that there is no gutter and it would only steal headline width.
      · ONE large graphic object holding the right side where the statistics
        grid used to be, with the middle-right left deliberately empty.
      · statistics demoted to a masthead credit strip in the base bar. The proof
        survives at a tenth of the visual weight. data/site.ts stats gained a
        `short` field for this ('Years', 'Events', 'Clients', 'Partners').
    aperture: >
      The intro's gold monogram ring, kept and grown ~100x. It is a DIAL, not a
      circle — outer rule, orbiting tick ring, counter-rotating inner arcs, one
      travelling marker — so it reads as a lens iris or stage-light gate rather
      than as generic circle decoration. Continuity with HeroIntro is the whole
      point; if that intro ever changes, revisit this.
    headline: >
      KineticHeadline reveals word by word out of a per-line overflow mask, each
      word lifting with rotateX so it arrives face-on rather than sliding. Once
      the words land, a specular highlight crosses the accent word.
    SPACE_NOT_MARGIN: >
      Word separation is a real space TEXT NODE, not mr-[0.24em]. The margin
      version looked identical and left the accessible name, the copied text and
      the indexable content reading "CreatingMoments,". Verified via innerText.
    SHEEN_DEGRADES_SAFELY: >
      .hero-sheen uses background-clip:text with FLAT gold at both ends of the
      gradient, so the word is solid gold at rest and stays solid gold if the
      animation never runs. That is why it needs no [data-motion="on"] guard,
      unlike the reveal rules. Do not "simplify" the flat stops away.
      It is clipped to the glyphs on purpose — a blended overlay band was tried
      first and washed across the background.
    responsive_headline: >
      The LINE BREAK caps the type size, so there are two. Below sm one word per
      line makes the longest word the constraint and the column carries 67.6px;
      the two-line version could only reach 39px there. Switched with
      useMediaQuery (now exported from lib/hooks), which resolves FALSE on the
      server — so the two-line version ships in the HTML and is the safe branch.
    pointer: >
      lib/usePointerParallax.ts is ONE window listener feeding motion values
      that the backdrop spotlight, the dial and the headline all read. It returns
      motion values, not state: useState there would re-render the whole hero on
      every mouse move. Headline leans into the cursor, dial leans away.
    verified: >
      tsc clean, next build clean (21/21). Home 16.9 kB / 196 kB first load
      (+2 kB for the whole rebuild).
      1440x820: 2 lines at 136px, longest line ends 41px inside the container,
      section exactly 820, rail bottom 772, spine clears the headline by 36px.
      1280x720 and 1024x768 likewise exact, 50px and 30px of headline clearance.
      375x812: 4 lines at 67.6px (was 39px), section exactly 812, CTA full-width.
      320x640: 57.6px, no x-overflow.
      Contrast raised where measured under AA: eyebrow ordinal gold/60 -> /85
      (4.39 -> 5.19 over the brightest plum), rail ordinals /70 -> /80 (4.77),
      spine white/45 -> /55 (5.25).
    NOT_verified: >
      None of the animation has been seen. rAF does not fire in this browser,
      so every geometry number above was measured with opacity and transform
      force-overridden via injected CSS. Also note matchMedia `change` events do
      NOT fire on programmatic resize in this pane (confirmed: 0 change events,
      0 resize events, while mql.matches read correctly) — the headline break
      only re-evaluates on reload here. A real browser resize fires both.
    revert_how: >
      Delete HeroAperture / KineticHeadline / usePointerParallax, restore the
      2026-08-04 "hero-scroll-collision-fix" Hero.tsx and HeroBackdrop from the
      transcript, and drop the hero blocks from globals.css.

  - id: hero-scroll-collision-fix
    date: 2026-08-04
    decision: >
      Home hero parallax rewritten. All foreground blocks share one pixel-based
      motion value (`drift` = { y, opacity }); the ground is the slower layer.
      Travel is deliberately small: ground 90px, content 28px.
    status: current
    why: >
      Reported on sight — "this is horrible as i scroll". The copy column had
      `y: 0 -> 42%` and the rail below it had none, so mid-scroll the copy slid
      into the rail and CTAs, stats, rail, scroll cue and location line piled
      into one band. Promoted to a contract: see contracts.parallax_units.
    also: >
      contentOpacity holds full until 15% of the hero's scroll range, so the
      rail is not dimming while it is still the main thing on screen.
      The StrokeText etch now shares that fade — it used to stay fully visible
      after the rest of the hero had gone, leaving a lone outlined word.
      The backdrop was resized to -top-[15%] h-[135%] so 90px of travel never
      exposes bare section background at either edge.
    revert_how: >
      Restore per-element transforms in components/home/Hero.tsx. Do not.

  - id: services-header-refined
    date: 2026-08-04
    decision: >
      components/home/ServicesSectionHeader.tsx: the seven-icon chain
      (SevenMarkIndex) is REMOVED. A single vertical gold hairline closing on a
      small lozenge (DescenderRule) takes its place, and the StrokeText etch
      moved from the top of the header to sit centred behind the headline.
      StrokeText gained a `sizeClassName` prop.
    status: current
    why: >
      Reported alongside the hero. Two faults. The etch sat at -top-4, putting a
      band of 12vw outlined capitals straight through a row of 17px icons joined
      by gold hairlines — two fine-line drawings at similar weights overlapping,
      which read as a tangle. And the chain was a THIRD copy of the same list:
      the seven cards are directly below it and the hero now carries a numbered
      index of the same practices.
    etch_sizing: >
      At the default 12vw the band is 126px tall against a 61px headline, so it
      spilled onto the eyebrow above and the paragraph below whatever it was
      centred on. It is now 8vw at lg, and the default is unchanged for the
      gallery masthead which genuinely wants a full-width band.
      If you place StrokeText behind a specific headline, size it DOWN.
    ornament_choice: >
      Vertical, because it is the only vertical rule on the page — a horizontal
      rule-and-diamond would have echoed StatementBand two sections later.
    verified: >
      Desktop 1280: ornament ends 906, eyebrow 942-959, etch 983-1067, h2
      995-1056 (etch centred on it exactly), paragraph from 1100. 24px and 33px
      of clearance. Mobile 385: etch 1039-1079 sits fully INSIDE the h2 at
      1023-1096. No collisions, no x-overflow. Header now contains one <svg>
      (the CTA arrow) where it previously had eight.
    dead_import_removed: components/home/ServicesGrid.tsx imported StrokeText and never used it.
    revert_how: >
      SevenMarkIndex is in the transcript for 2026-08-04. Note it also used
      getIcon / verticalList / useInViewOnce / useRef, whose imports were
      dropped with it.

  - id: marquee-removed
    date: 2026-08-03
    decision: >
      The scrolling marquee is GONE and should not come back. Both
      components/ui/MarqueeBand.tsx and components/ui/Marquee.tsx are deleted,
      along with the .animate-marquee / .marquee-track CSS and the @keyframes.
    status: current
    why: >
      Rejected on sight. It sat directly under seven video-backed service tiles
      and competed with them — after that much motion the page needs a breath,
      not a ticker. It also read as a generic template device rather than
      anything luxury.
      NOTE the original build brief asked for an "infinite marquee"; the user's
      later instruction supersedes it. If a future session re-reads that brief,
      do not helpfully rebuild this.
    replaced_by: >
      components/home/StatementBand.tsx — a still, centred editorial statement
      between ServicesGrid and AboutTeaser. Copy does real work: it explains
