      standard from a hundred-guest sangeeth to a thousand-person festival.")
      and hands the reader to the founder story. Only motion is a line-by-line
      mask reveal plus a self-drawing gold rule.
    also_changed: >
      It carries its own drawn rule, so the <SectionDivider /> that previously
      sat between ServicesGrid and AboutTeaser was removed — two rules stacked
      would have been redundant.
    verified: >
      Zero .marquee-track / .animate-marquee nodes remain. Statement band:
      3 reveal lines, 3 drawn rule paths, gold-deep accent (#887023).
      Contrast on ivory — headline 16.27, accent 4.54, subcopy 5.65, all pass.
      375px: headline 28px, fits, band 495px tall, no page overflow.
      Build clean, 21/21 static.

  - id: editorial-motion-pass
    date: 2026-08-03
    decision: >
      Added the four motion pieces that did not already exist: an alternating
      two-row marquee band, an outlined brand-phrase texture layer, an
      edge-to-edge drag carousel replacing the gallery grid, and parallax on the
      vertical hero videos. Hero headline scale raised on desktop.
    status: current
    already_existed: >
      Lenis, scroll-triggered reveals (SplitText/RevealText/stagger variants)
      and magnetic CTAs were requested again but were ALREADY implemented. Audit
      before rebuilding — most of the motion brief is done.
    added:
      - components/ui/MarqueeBand.tsx — REMOVED SAME DAY, see
        decisions.marquee-removed. Do not reintroduce.
      - components/ui/StrokeText.tsx + .brand-etch in globals.css — oversized
        stroke-only phrase behind section headers. Drifts on scroll.
      - components/gallery/DragCarousel.tsx — replaced the filterable masonry.
      - VerticalTemplate hero: backdrop 118% tall drifting 14% while copy
        drifts 40%; h1 up to xl:text-[6.5rem] (104px measured at 1280).

    TAILWIND_MERGE_ATE_TWO_CLASSES:
      severity: >
        Both were silent — the classes simply vanished from the DOM with no
        error. Worth knowing before adding any more custom utilities.
      case_1: >
        `.stroke-text` was stripped entirely. Tailwind owns the `stroke-*`
        namespace, so cn()/tailwind-merge treated `stroke-text` and
        `stroke-text-dark` as conflicting and kept only the last — the base
        class carrying the actual outline styling never rendered. Renamed to
        `.brand-etch` / `-dark` / `-light`, outside any Tailwind namespace.
        NOTE `outline-*` would have collided the same way.
      case_2: >
        `leading-[0.85]` was stripped when placed BEFORE `text-[18vw]`.
        tailwind-merge treats `text-<size>` as also setting line-height, so a
        later text-size drops an earlier leading. Fixed by ordering leading
        after the sizes. Measured line-height went 230px -> 126px.
      rule: >
        Custom utility classes must not start with a Tailwind namespace prefix,
        and `leading-*` must come after `text-<size>` inside one cn() call.

    carousel_design: >
      Built on a native overflow-x scroller, NOT a transform track. Touch keeps
      real momentum and scroll-chaining, keyboard gets arrow-key scrolling, and
      scroll-snap actually works. Desktop click-drag is layered on top by
      translating pointer movement into scrollLeft, with a >6px movement guard
      so a drag does not also fire the card's link.
    verified: >
      Carousel: 8 items, 4824px track vs 1265px viewport, snap-mandatory
      confirmed (set 1400 -> landed 1288), grab cursor, no zero-height images.
      375px: cards 323px, fit viewport, zero page overflow.
      MarqueeBand: 2 rows, directions normal/reverse, 42s/54s, aria-hidden.
      StrokeText: color transparent, 1.5px stroke, plum @22%, line-height ratio
      0.82. Hero h1 104px at 1280; backdrop 755px vs ~640px hero (118%).
      Typecheck and production build clean, 21/21 static.
    NOT_verified: >
      Hero parallax transforms read 0 — framer's useScroll depends on rAF, which
      this browser suspends, and Lenis intercepts programmatic scrollTo. The
      wiring is confirmed structurally (both layers wrapped in motion.div, 118%
      backdrop) but the drift has not been seen. Same for the marquee actually
      travelling and the stroke phrase drifting.
      Also: `pointer: fine` is true in this resized desktop browser even at
      375px, so the carousel showed "Drag"/grab there. On a real phone it will
      read "Swipe" with no grab cursor.

  - id: webgl-black-hole
    date: 2026-08-03
    decision: >
      three / @react-three/fiber / @react-three/drei are installed, and
      components/three/BlackHoleScene.tsx renders a real WebGL accretion disc
      behind the charcoal StatsBand (Home + About).
    status: current
    what_it_is: >
      6000 additive points on Keplerian orbits — inner rings sweep faster than
      outer ones, which is what reads as gravity rather than a spinning texture.
      Colour ramps plum (rim) -> gold -> near-white (horizon) in the fragment
      shader. One draw call; all animation is on the GPU, no per-frame CPU work.
      A charcoal sphere occludes the core.
    NOT_a_replacement: >
      components/ui/BlackHoleTransition.tsx (2D canvas) still exists and is
      still used — it is the hero's one-shot first-load collapse/burst. The
      WebGL scene is a persistent ambient background. Different jobs; keep both.
    loading: >
      next/dynamic ssr:false AND gated on the band scrolling into view, so the
      three.js runtime is never on any critical path and a visitor who never
      reaches the stats never downloads it. Refuses to mount at all under
      prefers-reduced-motion — no WebGL context is created.
    CANVAS_SIZING_GOTCHA: >
      <Canvas> applies style/className to its CONTAINER; the inner <canvas> is
      sized by a ResizeObserver. Where that observer is slow or absent the
      canvas sits at its 300x150 default. globals.css therefore pins
      [data-webgl-stage] > div and its canvas to 100%/100%. Harmless where the
      observer works.
    TYPE_FALLOUT_FROM_INSTALL: >
      Installing R3F broke components/ui/SplitText.tsx. @react-three/fiber
      augments React's JSX.IntrinsicElements with every three.js object, so
      SplitText's `as?: ElementType` resolved to an enormous union and the props
      collapsed to `never`. Fixed by constraining it to a `TextTag` union
      ('h1'|'h2'|'h3'|'h4'|'p'|'div'|'span'). If another polymorphic component
      is added, expect the same and constrain it the same way.
    verified: >
      Canvas mounts with a real webgl2 context on the GPU
      (ANGLE / Intel Iris Xe / D3D11) and fills the band (1265x312).
      Typecheck and production build clean, 21/21 static.
    NOT_verified: >
      The disc has not been SEEN rendering. readPixels returns zeros without
      preserveDrawingBuffer, and the backing store stayed at 300x150 here
      because ResizeObserver does not fire in this browser — so shader output,
      orbital motion and final resolution are all unconfirmed. Needs a human
      look on real hardware.

