        unescaped one is parsed as a filter separator, which is exactly how an
        earlier inline attempt failed.
    scrim_left_shared: >
      I started building a per-clip scrim knob on the belief that the gym
      footage was much darker than the others — the poster frame looked it.
      MEASURED PROPERLY (8 frames sampled per clip) the three are within ~8
      luma of each other: celebrations 101.9, fitness 100.6, corporate 93.6.
      The premise was wrong, so no knob was added and the shared scrim stands.
      Single-frame luminance is not a usable proxy for a clip.
    payload_now: >
      Hero video totals across the three: 2700 KB desktop / 1628 KB mobile.
      Only one hero loads per page view, so the per-page cost is one clip.
    verified: >
      Mounted with the correct file and 8s duration, readyState 4, faded in,
      play() resolves with no error. Poster-path audit confirms exactly three
      verticals on video and four still on unsplash stills. 375px: mobile cut,
      375x617 object-cover, h1 33.6px fits, 56px CTA, zero overflow.
      Build clean, 21/21.
    NOT_verified: >
      Fitness playback was NOT observed advancing or looping. The AI session's
      tab reported document.hidden = true throughout, which suspends media
      advance; play() resolved and readyState stayed 4, but currentTime froze.
      Corporate and all seven card clips WERE observed looping earlier through
