  - id: lottie-services-grid
    date: 2026-08-02
    decision: >
      The home services grid is components/home/ServicesGrid.tsx — a 7-card
      Lottie-driven grid. It REPLACED components/home/VerticalsGrid.tsx, which
      was deleted.
    status: current
    revert_to: snapshots["2026-08-02-pre-lottie"]
    revert_how: >
      Copy components/home/VerticalsGrid.tsx back from that snapshot, change the
      import + usage in app/page.tsx from ServicesGrid to VerticalsGrid, delete
      components/home/ServicesGrid.tsx, and optionally
      `npm uninstall lottie-react` and remove public/lottie/. Nothing else on
      the site imports any of it.
    added:
      - dependency lottie-react@2.4.1
      - public/lottie/*.json — 7 PLACEHOLDER animations, procedurally generated,
        abstract motifs only. NOT the specced character silhouettes. Overwrite
        each file in place; no code change needed.
      - components/home/ServicesGrid.tsx
    per_card_behaviour:
      celebrations: ambient — slow continuous loop, speed 0.35, hover does nothing
      corporate: hoverSequence — holds frame 0, plays forward on hover, reverses on leave
      fitness: hoverSequence — grounded pose, leaps on hover
      adventure: loop + GSAP scale on the card backdrop on hover
      entertainment: loop + Tailwind radial-gradient DJ lights that fade in on hover
      community: hoverSequence — figures converge, ring pops
      workshops: hoverSequence — idea particles radiate outward
    critical_notes:
      - lottie-react is loaded via next/dynamic ssr:false. It touches `document`
        at module scope and WILL break SSR if imported normally.
      - The imperative handle comes through the component's own `lottieRef`
        PROP, never a React ref. next/dynamic does not forward refs — a ref
        would silently be null and every hover interaction would no-op.
      - lottie-react wants parsed `animationData`, not a URL. The JSON is
        fetched in useLottieDocument and validated (`Array.isArray(doc.layers)`)
        so a 404 served as HTML cannot reach the renderer.
      - If the JSON is missing or malformed the card falls back to its lucide
        icon — i.e. the previous design. It never renders an empty badge. This
        is deliberate; blank-content bugs have shipped twice on this project.
      - Fetching is gated on an IntersectionObserver so seven payloads stay off
        the critical path.
    verified: >
      All 7 files serve 200 with valid layer counts; with the viewport gate
      temporarily bypassed, all 7 badges rendered real lottie-web SVGs
      (viewBox 0 0 200 200, g-counts matching each file's layers). Fallback path
      confirmed working too. Production build clean, 21/21 static.
    NOT_verified: >
      No hover interaction and no animation playback has been observed — the AI
      session's browser does not composite frames, so IntersectionObserver never
      fires and requestAnimationFrame is frozen. The idle-frame holds, the
      forward/reverse hover sequences, the GSAP zoom and the DJ lights are all
      unwatched.

