    1440x820, 1280x720, 1024x768, 768x1024 and 375x812, with no headline wrap
    at any of them. Vertical service heroes: all seven at 68px on two lines,
    clearance to the overlapping white panel 87px at 1280x650 and a proven
    32px floor at any height.
  how_to_check_a_headline_wrapped: >
    Compare the two line boxes' heights — equal means neither wrapped. The
    widest-word measurement does NOT catch it, because a wrapped line still
    reports every word inside the column. This cost two wrong passes.
  measure_dont_eyeball: >
    Several confident claims made this project were disproved by measuring:
    a card description that "failed" contrast passed at 5.74, footage that
    looked much darker than its siblings was within 8 luma over 8 sampled
    frames, and video stalls blamed on document.visibilityState were actually
    fixed by retrying. Measure contrast, luminance, seams and box geometry.
  NOT_verified: >
