## 2026-08-14 — Community: photographs added to the burst circles

**THE BRIEF'S ASSET MAPPING WAS WRONG IN THREE WAYS — all silent locally.**
Files on disk were `apartment events.jpeg`, `women meetups.jpeg`,
`pet meetups.jpeg`, `family days.jpeg`, `festivals.jpeg`:
 1. All LOWERCASE. The brief gave `Apartment events` / `Pet meetups` /
    `Festivals` with capitals. A capitalised path resolves on Windows
    (case-insensitive) and 404s on the Linux host that serves production — the
    worst kind of bug, invisible until deploy.
 2. Family Days maps to `family days`, NOT `Family meetups` as the brief said.
 3. All `.jpeg`, not the `.png`/`.jpg` the brief anticipated.
Plus every filename contained a SPACE, which needs percent-encoding in a URL.
Renamed all five to kebab-case `community-*.jpg` — kills the space and the case
ambiguity in one move, and matches every other asset in the project.

**Optimised on the way through:** 1600x893 originals at 315-546KB, rendering into
216-264px circles. Resized to 900px wide, mozjpeg q80: 2150KB -> 355KB total,
an 83% cut. Originals left on disk (unreferenced) rather than deleted — no VCS,
so destroying client uploads is not mine to do; flagged for removal.

**THE SPIN THAT NEVER UNWINDS.** Animating `rotate` to 360 on hover and back to 0
on leave spins the card BACKWARDS on the way out — the "snapping" the brief
rules out. Instead the turn runs once and, the instant it completes,
`rotate.set(0)` fires WITHOUT animating. 360° and 0° are the same picture, so
nothing moves, and a later mouse-leave has nothing left to unwind. A `spinning`
ref keeps re-entry from restarting it mid-turn.

**Hover moved to an inner element.** The <li> is already driven by the burst's
hidden/shown variants; a second variant system on the same node would fight it.
The split also lets the hover PROPAGATE by name to the image, which is what
drives the 1.15 zoom under the text.

**CONTRAST FAILED FIRST TIME AND MEASUREMENT CAUGHT IT.** With the brief's
`from-black/50 via-black/70 to-black/90`, worst case over a white photo: numerals
2.88-3.40:1 — all five under AA. Cause: the numeral sits highest in the circle
where the gradient is weakest (alpha 0.59) AND was a 300-level pastel; a light
tint on a mid-grey has almost no separation. Fixed by strengthening the top stop
to /65 and lifting accents to 200-level. After: numerals 5.76-6.34, titles
10.05-10.37, descriptions 12.63. Icons share the numeral's colour and sit BELOW
it (darker scrim), so their contrast is strictly higher than 5.76 — well past the
3:1 non-text threshold.

**Verified:** 5 circles, all renamed images 200 (raw and through
`/_next/image`), correct title->photo mapping, rowLayout [3,2] desktop and
[1,1,1,1,1] mobile, `offsetsCorrect: true` (burst deltas still match each
circle's true distance from centre after the rewrite), perfectly round, overflow
hidden, gradient present, `sizes` honoured with a 16w-3840w ladder so a 216px
circle fetches 640w rather than the 3840w fallback that appears in `src`.
`tsc` clean; `next build` clean 21/21, /services/[slug] 35.7 kB / 209 kB.

**Build flakiness, fourth occurrence and worst yet:** `next build` failed with
ALL THREE fonts (`Inter`, `Outfit`, `Playfair Display`) unfetchable. Curled
