**`perspective` ON THE ANCESTOR.** Declared on the transformed node it does
nothing and the tilt flattens to a skew. Verified `perspective: 1000px` on the
<section>, with the tilt on the child.

**Sprung the SOURCE, not each output.** Two raw pointer values sprung once and
shared by both rotations; springing each axis separately lets them drift apart
mid-motion, which reads as the folder flexing rather than tilting.

**Folders do not close on mouse-leave.** Closing on leave makes the section
flicker as the pointer crosses it; both open by default so nobody arrives at two
blank covers. Click toggles, so touch can still collapse one.

**COVER TEXT: DROPPED HALF THE BRIEFED STRING.** The brief's foil line is
`SKILL BUILDING · WORKSHOPS`, but with a serif title beneath it that prints
