**NEARLY REPORTED A FALSE BUG ON THE CENTREPIECE.** The backdrop appeared frozen
at `/wellness-dance.jpg` for every card. Cause: the cross-fade keeps every layer
mounted (exits need frames, which this hidden pane never gives), SEVEN had
accumulated, and my selector read the FIRST img — the oldest. React also reuses a
key when the same image is reselected, so DOM order cannot identify the current
one at all. Added `data-reveal` / `data-reveal-for` mirroring the selected image,
which states it independently of animation: all seven cards then verified to
drive their own image, `everyCardDrivesItsOwnImage: true`.
RULE EXTENDED: when a cross-fade keeps N layers alive, neither "first" nor
"last" in DOM order is the current one — expose the state instead of inferring
it from the DOM.

**Verified:** 2 folders, 7 cards, both open, 2-column split, zero white panels,
Ken Burns applied, foil labels 9.69 / 9.27:1, card title 12.16:1, desc 12.15:1.
Mobile 375: single column, all 7 cards, every tap target >= 44px (60-102), no
