## 2026-08-14 — Community: coin drop + hover reveal

Replaces the centre-burst with a coin drop and moves all copy behind hover.
Deleted the entire offset-measurement apparatus (offsetLeft/offsetTop,
useAnimationControls, controls.set) — a coin drop needs no per-card geometry, so
that machinery went with it.

**BOUNCE CONVERTED TO PHYSICS RATHER THAN PASSED ALONGSIDE THEM.** The brief asked
for `bounce: 0.4, damping: 12, mass: 1.2`, but framer reads a spring EITHER as
physics (stiffness/damping/mass) OR as duration+bounce — mixing lets one branch
silently win and the other be ignored. Converted instead:
  bounce 0.4 -> damping ratio Z ~= 0.6;  Z = damping / (2*sqrt(k*mass));
  0.6 = 12 / (2*sqrt(k*1.2))  ->  k ~= 83.
Passed as one coherent set: stiffness 83, damping 12, mass 1.2.

**SPIN STAYS IMPERATIVE — deviation from the briefed variant structure, restated.**
As `rest: rotate 0` / `hover: rotate 360`, framer animates 360 -> 0 on leave and
the card visibly spins BACKWARDS every time. Zero-duration rest fixes that but
snaps if the pointer leaves mid-turn. Imperative: the turn always completes,
then `rotate.set(0)` with no animation — 360° and 0° are the same picture, so
nothing moves, the value really is 0, and it repeats cleanly. CONTENT still uses
the parent/child variant orchestration the brief describes.

**TWO REAL BUGS FOUND BY MEASURING THE DEFAULT STATE, both from the same root.**
Hiding all copy behind hover is a desktop-only idea, and `usePointerFine`
resolves in an EFFECT, not on first render:
 1. `initial` derived from it was computed from the wrong value, so every card
    mounted with content at opacity 1 and faded out once the query settled — a
    flash of all five cards' copy on every page load. Measured: children had
    inline `opacity:1` at rest.
 2. `usePointerFine`'s unresolved value is `false` = "cannot hover", which is
    backwards for this use. Wrote `useTouchPointer` around `pointer: coarse`
    instead, whose unresolved value means "assume it CAN hover" — so the first
    paint is hidden on every device and only a confirmed touch screen opts out.
 3. Even then, touch reached the revealed state only by ANIMATING there, making
    the titles — the only copy touch users get — dependent on an animation
    running. Keyed the subtree on pointer type so touch REMOUNTS already
    revealed. Nothing to animate, nothing to fail.
Verified both: pointer `ONLY_PHOTO_VISIBLE: true` (img 1, overlay 0, bloom 0,
content 0); touch `CONTENT_VISIBLE_ON_TOUCH: true` (all four at 1).

**Verified:** 5 coins, correct title->photo mapping, coin-drop initial
`opacity:0; translateY(-420px)` identical on all five, rowLayout [3,2] desktop /
5x1 mobile, perfect circles, `object-fit: cover`, no sideways scroll. `tsc`
clean.

**RULE, third time this pattern has bitten:** a media-query hook that resolves in
an effect must have its UNRESOLVED value chosen so the first paint is the safe
state. Phrase the query so that "unknown" and "safe" coincide, rather than
correcting after mount.

