**COPY WENT INTO `longDesc`, NOT THE COMPONENT.** The brief's descriptions are
longer than the existing `desc`, and `VerticalService.longDesc` already exists
for exactly this ("longer, more evocative copy... `desc` stays the short form").
Copy belongs in data.

**THE BUG THIS TURN: `String.find()` HIT THE WRONG VERTICAL.** My insert script
located each service by `title:` and used the FIRST match — but "Wellness
Retreats" exists TWICE in the file, once in Fitness (line 754) and once in
Workshops (line 1037), and Fitness comes first. So workshop copy was written
onto a FITNESS service, and the workshops card silently kept rendering its short
desc. Caught by diffing every rendered description against the brief: 6 of 7
matched, one did not. Fixed by targeting the unique `desc` string instead of the
ambiguous title, then AUDITED ALL SEVEN by comparing each longDesc's line number
against the workshops block start — the other seven longDesc entries in the file
are pre-existing celebrations copy, confirmed by reading their content.
Verified Fitness is undamaged: keeps its own copy, no workshop text leaked.
RULE: in a file where titles repeat across sections, never anchor an edit on a
title. Anchor on something unique to the target, and verify placement by
position afterwards.

**Blur is on the IMAGE, not a backdrop-filter.** A `backdrop-filter` on a layer
above would also blur the folders sitting on top of it — which are the one thing
that must stay sharp.

