## 2026-08-15 — /services rebuilt as the Category Vaults

Fourth design for this page. Five vault rows, exactly one open, sub-services in
a responsive grid inside the open vault, ambient lighting keyed to the active
vault.

**ONE IMPLEMENTATION AT EVERY WIDTH — a deliberate reading of the brief.** It
describes a desktop matrix and a mobile stack as separate things, and building
them separately is exactly what lets one rot: the mobile path only gets
exercised when someone remembers to look. A single accordion whose interior
grid reflows 1 -> 2 -> 3 columns is the same design at every size, so a phone
cannot receive a layout a desktop never tested. This is also the direct answer
to the brief's own "eliminates horizontal overflow / text clipping / broken
grids on small viewports".

**EXACTLY ONE VAULT OPEN, ALWAYS.** A vault that could also close would let the
reader reach five closed bars with no services and no active vault for the
ambient lighting to key off. Clicking the open vault keeps it open. Verified
across all five plus a re-click: `alwaysExactlyOneOpen: true`.

**DEVIATED FROM THE BRIEF'S `layout` PROP — different reason from last time.**
Framer performs layout animations by SCALING, and a scaled box squashes its own
text for the duration unless every child counter-animates. On an accordion
whose entire payload is type, that distortion lands on exactly what the reader
is watching arrive. Animated `height: 'auto'` with the brief's exact spring
(300/30) instead — same motion, nothing to distort. (Last turn's `layout`
deviation was the rotate conflict; this one is text scaling. Both real, but not
the same problem.)

**FIXED A REAL ARIA DEFECT:** closed vaults pointed `aria-controls` at a panel
that no longer exists, because the panel unmounts. A dangling reference is
worse than none — `aria-expanded` already says there is nothing to jump to.
Now set only while the panel is mounted; verified 0 dangling across every state.

**REAL CONTRAST FAILURE FOUND AND FIXED:** the closed vault numeral at
`rgba(255,255,255,0.28)` measured 2.36:1 — under even the 3:1 allowance for
large text, on an element carrying the vault's identity. Raised to 0.46 for
4.58:1. The open state still reads at roughly twice that, so the hierarchy
survives.

**Final contrast, all five foils measured individually:** open numerals
6.57-9.46, badges 6.25-9.00, card titles 18.93, card bodies 9.48, closed
numeral 4.58. AA throughout against a pure-white photograph under all four
scrims.

**NEW PROBE TRAP — CSS TRANSITIONS ARE FROZEN TOO, not just framer.** The open
vault's numeral read as the CLOSED colour while `data-open` said true, which
looked exactly like a state bug. React had set the inline style correctly to
`rgb(197,168,128)`; the COMPUTED value was stuck because `transition-colors
duration-500` never advances without frames. Setting `transition: none` and
forcing a recalc returned the right colour immediately. Any future colour
measurement in this pane must disable transitions first, or it measures the
previous state.

**Overflow verified with ALL FIVE PANELS OPEN at 320px** — the frozen exits
made this a stricter test than intended, since all 20 cards render at once. No
self-clipping, no escapes, nothing off-viewport, no horizontal page overflow.
Also clean at 1440.

**All 7 verticals confirmed reachable — observed, not inferred this time.**
Opening each vault in turn accumulated through-links to celebrations,
corporate, fitness, workshops, adventure, entertainment, community.

**THREE DEAD COMPONENTS NOW: ServicesHub, MasterCarousel, ChapterFeed.** All
unused, all kept only because there is still no version control. Four designs
for one page in one session, three surviving only as clutter. This is now the
clearest cost of no VCS in the repo.

## 2026-08-15 — Navbar overflow fix + mood-matched vault artwork

### Navbar: the bug is REAL, and it is FONT-DEPENDENT

Reproduced properly rather than patched on report. At 1024 the row needs 933px
and has 961 — it fits, but the webfont is the only thing paying for the 28px of
margin. Forcing the generic fallbacks the browser uses when the font never
arrives:

    Inter      933  (+28)
    Segoe UI   915  (+46)
    Arial      972  (-11)   <- overflows
    Verdana    980  (-19)   <- overflows

That is why every previous measurement this session reported
`horizontalOverflow: false`: the pane always had Inter loaded. And this project
has failed to fetch its font from fonts.gstatic.com at build time REPEATEDLY,
so a fallback render is a live path, not a hypothesis.

**THE BRIEF'S PRESCRIBED FIX WOULD HAVE MADE IT WORSE.** It asks for
`gap-4 lg:gap-8`; the nav currently uses `gap-1`, so that adds ~50px of gap to
a row already 19px short. Said so and fixed the actual cause instead:
compressed padding/tracking between 1024 and 1279 (`px-2.5`, `tracking-.14em`,
`gap-0.5`, CTA `px-4 ml-1`) and restored the original comfortable values from
`xl` up. Worst-case fallback now has +46px at 1024, and +251px at 1280 where
the original spacing is back. Verified `xl` really does restore: padding 12px,
tracking 1.76px, gap 4px.

Also adopted the brief's `max-w-7xl w-full box-border` in place of Tailwind's
`container`. Same 1280 ceiling in practice, but explicit.

**The hamburger already existed and already triggered below `lg`** — verified
rather than rebuilt: at 1023 the desktop nav is `display:none`, the button is
44x44, the drawer opens with 8 links, body scroll locks, and nothing overflows.

### Vault artwork

**LOCAL, NOT UNSPLASH — deliberate.** The brief allows either. Remote heroes in
this project have produced `upstream image response timed out` and 500s on
service routes, because next/image proxies them at request time and a slow
origin becomes a failed page rather than a slow one.

Re-matched by subject to each vault's brief:
  weddings   sangeeth stage      -> /image_3.png (celebrations' own Weddings art)
  corporate  unchanged           -> the keynote floor already matched
  fitness    zumba class         -> yoga-foundations (the pavilion)
  adventure  treks               -> expedition-camping (the camp, not the trail)
  production concert             -> performance-dj (the rig with lasers/haze)

**MATCHED BY FILENAME AND EXISTING USAGE, NOT BY LOOKING.** Stated plainly to
the user — I cannot see these images, and a confident-sounding mood claim I
cannot verify is worse than an honest caveat.

**Adopted the brief's gradient exactly** — `bg-gradient-to-t from-[#050505]
via-[#050505]/80 to-transparent` — replacing the flat 88% scrim. `to-transparent`
leaves the TOP of the viewport unscrimmed, which is normally where a headline
goes blind, so this is only safe because the artwork sits at 18%: worst case a
pure-white photo lands the ground at rgb(50,50,50) and the h1 still measures
12.82:1. The two numbers are a PAIR — raising image opacity invalidates the
gradient. Noted in the code.

Contrast after the change, AAA throughout: h1 12.82, hero lede 7.20, vault
title 19.68, card title 18.90, card body 9.46. Min 7.20.

**Verified:** all five files 200, five distinct assets, 5/5 decoded, 0 broken.

**REMEMBERED THE TRANSITION TRAP** from the previous entry — disabled all CSS
transitions before measuring colour, since they freeze mid-flight here and
would report the previous state.

**New probe trap:** `document.querySelector('header')` matches the SITE NAVBAR,
not the page's own header — it is first in the DOM. Cost one failed probe;
scope to the component root and use `header:not([data-site-header])`.

