Fifth design for this page. Five tiles in an asymmetric bento, full-bleed art,
gold/purple foil badges, sub-services gliding in on hover/focus.

**THE BENTO TESSELLATES — verified, not eyeballed.** On three columns:

    [ 01  01  02 ]
    [ 01  01  03 ]
    [ 04  05  05 ]

4 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 2 = 9 in 3x3, no holes. Measured at 1280: tile 01 at 803x624
spanning 2x2, 02/03 stacked in column 3, 04 then 05 (803 wide) on row 3. Three
distinct row tops, three column lefts, coverage 91.2% — exactly 100% minus the
24px gaps.

**TILE 05 DELIBERATELY DOES NOT SPAN AT `md`.** Two columns with 01 spanning
gives 2+1+1+1+1 = 6 in 3x2, also exact. Had 05 kept its span there, a two-wide
tile following three singles would have stranded a hole on the last row.
Verified at 768: every row full, no gaps.

**NAVBAR — NOTHING TO DO, and I checked rather than re-fixed it.** Last turn's
work already holds: `max-w-7xl w-full box-border`, hamburger below `lg`,
+46px spare at 1024 on the worst font fallback. Re-fixing a fixed thing risks
undoing it.

**HOVER IS AN ENHANCEMENT, NEVER THE ONLY ROUTE.** The panel opens on hover OR
focus, and permanently on touch — a touch device has no hover, so anything
gated behind it is simply absent on a phone, and the through-links live inside
