which is exactly why the background decision below matters.

THE NAVBAR BACKGROUND IS OPAQUE, NOT THE BRIEF'S `/90`.
On a light page `bg-[#F9F9FB]/90` is indistinguishable from opaque. Over an
obsidian hero it blends down to rgb(225,225,227), a DIFFERENT ground — and the
gold hover falls from 4.55:1 to 4.08:1 and fails AA. Solving for the alpha that
keeps gold at 4.5:1 over obsidian gives ~0.996, i.e. opaque anyway. So the bar
carries its own ground and every figure below is a CONSTANT rather than a
function of whatever is scrolled underneath. Same principle that fixed the
