The brief asked for #C5A880 in two places. Measured on these grounds it is
2.15:1 on the bar and 2.21:1 on the cream page; #DFC298 is 1.85:1. All three
are below even the 3:1 LARGE-text floor, so the "Dream Event" accent — the word
the whole left column is built around — would have been the least readable
thing on the page. #887023 is not an invention: the @theme block already added
it for exactly this case, recording that the brand gold measures 2.0:1 on
ivory. It reads 4.67:1 on the cream and 4.55:1 on the bar. Pale gold is kept
where it is NOT text.

Also plum-not-gold on the contact tab hover, for the same reason (gold would
have been 2.2:1 on the ivory track); the submit button is plum resting with a
GOLD hover carrying charcoal text, matching the nav's Book Event so the primary
action behaves the same everywhere. White-on-gold would be ~1.9:1.

ONE PURPLE, NOT TWO. The brief specified #3A225F; `--color-smaya-plum` is
#3d1f5c and is already used by the footer, mega menu and every CTA. The two are
visually indistinguishable, so the token wins — a second near-identical purple
