================================================================================
2026-08-15 — home statement copy + /testimonials editorial showcase
================================================================================

HOME (components/home/StatementBand.tsx). Copy swap only, structure untouched.
Re-split across the three RevealText lines so the mask reveal still lands one
line at a time, and moved the gold italic accent onto "curtain-up" — the accent
is the closing word of the headline by design, and dropping it would have left
the drawn rule above pointing at nothing. Verified in the DOM: new headline and
new paragraph present, all three old phrases gone.

/TESTIMONIALS — SIX COLUMNS, NOT THREE. That is the whole trick.

The brief asked for `lg:grid-cols-3` with a spotlight spanning two columns. A
3-column track can only ever be thirds, so 5 normal cards + 1 double = 7 column
units against a 3-column grid: the last row holds ONE card and two holes. That
reads as a broken grid, not as editorial asymmetry.

A 6-column track divides into 4+2, 2+4 and 3+3 — three DIFFERENT row
compositions that all come out flush:
  row 1  [---- spotlight ----][ half ]
  row 2  [ half ][---- spotlight ----]   <- mirrored
  row 3  [  third  ][  third  ]
MEASURED at 1009px: 630+299, 299+630, 464+464 — every row totals 928-929.
Zero holes, and genuinely asymmetric.

Indexed `% LAYOUT.length` so data/testimonials.ts can grow without touching the
component; rows stay flush at multiples of six and a remainder leaves a short
final row rather than a broken one. Spans are whole literal class strings —
Tailwind v4 scans statically, so `lg:col-span-${n}` would never be generated.

CONTRAST FIX FOUND WHILE REBUILDING: the client designation was
`text-smaya-charcoal/45`, which blends to rgb(153,153,154) on white and
measures 2.85:1 — under AA, on the only line that tells you WHO is speaking.
Now plum at 13.34:1, which is also what the brief asked for.
Measured on this page: quote 15.13, author 17.13, designation 13.34, h1 16.72.

KNOWN AND FLAGGED (same class as the contact input border): the gold stars are
`smaya-gold` #d4af37 at 2.10:1 on white, under the 3:1 WCAG 1.4.11 wants for a
meaningful graphic. Kept because it is the site's signature gold and every
other page uses it — and the rating is redundantly available as text via
`role="img" aria-label="Rated 5 out of 5"` on the group, with the five
individual stars aria-hidden so a screen reader gets one object rather than
five nameless graphics. A gold that clears 3:1 needs to go to about #A8842A.
The card's gold-foil border at 1.26:1 is decorative and carries no information,
so it is not a 1.4.11 item.

RESPONSIVE, measured: 375 → 1 col, 335px cards, overflow 0, clipped 0.
753 → 2 cols, three flush rows of 340+340, overflow 0. 1009 → the 6-col rhythm
above, overflow 0, clipped 0. `min-w-0` on every grid item, because a grid
child defaults to `min-width:auto` and one long author name would otherwise
widen a track and start the page scrolling sideways.

BUILD STATUS: not built. The previous build attempt was killed by
fonts.gstatic.com ("socket hang up", retry loop) and the user asked for the dev
server instead. tsc --noEmit passes. Self-hosting the fonts remains unfixed and
is now the single highest-value outstanding item.


