--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RETRACTION: THE HOME PAGE HORIZONTAL OVERFLOW IS NOT A BUG.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
I have carried "home page horizontal scrollbar, 6px desktop / 10px mobile,
pre-existing" on the outstanding list for most of this session, having earlier
differential-tested it only far enough to prove the marquee was not the cause.
It is a FROZEN-rAF ARTIFACT of this preview pane.

Proof: 38 elements sit at their Framer `initial` transform (measured
`opacity:0; transform:translateX(-30px)` on the AboutTeaser column, with a
slideInRight sibling at +30px). Setting `transform:none` on all 38 takes
scrollWidth-clientWidth from 10 to 0; restoring the exact inline styles brings
it back to 10. Where rAF runs, those animate to x:0 on enter and there is no
overflow at all.

Note the near-miss: neutralising ONE element changed nothing (10 -> 10),
because the left-shifted and right-shifted columns each hold an edge. A
single-element test would have "disproved" the correct explanation.

