================================================================================
2026-08-15 — mobile responsiveness audit (320-768), route loading, pin fallback
================================================================================

METHOD NOTE FIRST, because it invalidated my own earlier probes.

  1. `body { overflow-x: hidden }` PROPAGATES TO THE VIEWPORT, and body itself
     then computes to `overflow: visible`. So body does NOT clip its children —
     it only suppresses the scrollbar. Two consequences: content can still sit
     past the viewport (scrollWidth reports it), and any probe that walks
     ancestors looking for an `overflow-x: hidden` clipper will match BODY for
     every element on the page and dutifully report zero offenders. Several of
     my "unclippedOverflowNodes: 0" readings earlier this session were vacuous
     for exactly that reason. Walk to the element's own clipping ancestor,
     excluding body, or measure `right > clientWidth` directly.

  2. Stuck Framer `initial` transforms must be REMOVED, not set to
     `transform:none`, and ALL of them at once. Setting one to none left the
     10px on /about unchanged and I nearly recorded a real bug; removing every
     inline style carrying a translate took it to 0. Same near-miss as the home
     page: a left-shifted and a right-shifted element each hold one edge.

TWO REAL OVERFLOW BUGS FOUND AND FIXED (everything else at 320 was clean:
/, /events, /blog, /contact, /gallery, /testimonials, /about all 0):

  a. /services carousel controls, 5px. Two 44px arrows + 20px gaps + a 200px
     dot group = 328 of content inside a 280 container, children sitting at -4
     and 324. My original arithmetic was right FOR 375 and I never re-checked
     at 320, which is 55px tighter. Base metrics now 88+24+152 = 264 with 16px
     spare; `sm:` restores the roomier original; `flex-wrap` guards a future
     sixth division. Dots are 24x44 at base — exactly WCAG 2.5.8's 24px, with
     the 44px HEIGHT doing the ergonomic work.

  b. FeatureCarousel `w-[320px]`, and this one was INVISIBLE. A hardcoded 320px
     card inside a 280px column ran 40px past it, and an `overflow-x-clip`
     ancestor sliced the right-hand 40px off every slide — no scrollbar, no
     warning, just missing card. `max-w-full` caps it only where it does not
     fit. Verified the narrower card did not then overflow VERTICALLY inside
     its fixed height: scrollHeight 400 === clientHeight 400.

STAGEGALLERY: the 400vh pinned horizontal reel was gated on
`prefers-reduced-motion` ONLY, so a phone got four viewport-heights of vertical
scroll that merely slide a filmstrip sideways. Now CSS-gated at `md`, following
the principle WellnessShowcase already documents in this repo: CSS owns the
LAYOUT, JS owns only the wiring. A `matchMedia` branch would have to pick one
arrangement for the server HTML and correct itself after hydration — a visible
jump at whichever width guessed wrong. And `travel` needs no gate at all: it is
`track.scrollWidth - innerWidth`, and a column track is never wider than the
screen, so it resolves to 0 and `x` never moves.
  320:  pin static, track column, travel 0, cards 280 inside viewport, HUD none
  1265: wrapper 3600 = exactly 400vh, pin sticky, track row, travel 2159

iOS ZOOM — the highest-value fix here and invisible on desktop. Every contact
field was `text-sm` (14px); mobile Safari auto-zooms any focused control under
16px, so every tap yanked the page to ~114% and left it there. Now `text-base`
with `sm:text-sm`, since the zoom only applies to the small viewport anyway.
Verified: all five controls report 16px.

ROUTE LOADING. Added `loading.tsx` to all seven segments plus a shared neutral
RouteSkeleton, and explicit `prefetch` on all six navbar Links. HONEST SCOPE:
every route is already statically prerendered and next/link already prefetches
static routes, so a warm navigation resolves from the router cache and the
skeleton never paints. It earns its place on cold entry, hard reload, slow
connection, or a link tapped before its prefetch landed. The lag visible in
THIS session is dev-mode compilation (18-29s per route on first hit), which
does not exist in the production build.

NOT DONE, DELIBERATELY:
  - `overflow-x-hidden` on <html>. body already carries it and the pins work
    (verified StageGallery sticky at 1265). Adding it to html makes html the
    scroll container and is a known way to kill `position: sticky` silently —
    this site has five pinned sections riding on that.
  - Blanket `will-change: transform`. It is a memory hint, not a speed switch;
    applied broadly it costs a compositor layer per element and can make a long
    page slower. Framer already promotes the elements it animates.

VERIFIED CLEAN: 8 routes at 320 -> 0 overflow; mobile drawer 9 targets, none
under 44px, body scroll locked; no rigid text-5xl+ heading anywhere lacking a
responsive step-down (typography scaling was already correct).
